00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.470 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  at long last the black widow solo movie  has arrived and natasha romanov is  getting her time in the spotlight  in addition to potentially laying the  groundwork for future stories  the prequel also offers a few sly winks  at the mcu  and marvel comics here are some easter  eggs you missed in black widow  when black widow moves to its present  day timeline of 2016  our title hero is on the run from  probably the busiest  secretary of state in us history retired  general thaddeus thunderbolt ross who's  convinced he's got her pinned  down natasha calls ross on his cell  warning him not to embarrass himself  it turns out that she's on a ferry in  norway which at best puts ross  six time zones and a continent away as  nat  settles into her new home courtesy of  her ally and supplier mason  she cracks a norwegian beer and settles  in to watch roger moore do his thing as  agent 07.  apparently she's a big enough james bond  fan to quote the film  line by line this easter egg comes in  the form of her movie of choice which  bond super fans will instantly recognize  as  moonraker there are some obvious  parallels between moonraker and black  widow both films feature an evil  megalomaniac bent on world domination  pulling strings from a remote base in  the sky a space station for moonraker  antagonist hugo drex and the hovering  red room installation of black widow big  bad  dracov both primary antagonists also  have a strong  and silent heavy drax chief henchman  jaws and dracov's daughter turned puppet  antonia  aka taskmaster who only speaks once  after their loyalty shifts  when his sleeper cell slash family  escapes the united states to cuba  alexi is thrilled after all he was the  red guardian the soviet union's first  and only super soldier  he had no business flying under the  radar in the american midwest stealing  secrets  he belongs on the battlefront  when natasha and elena rescue him from  prison he describes their time as a faux  family as  tedious and boring for which he tells an  obviously upset  elena he means no offense into writing  the only family she had ever known  as the movie goes on alexi's affections  for his fake daughters come out from  behind the gruff and rigid exterior he  shows the world  but viewers paying close attention to  his tattoos could have reached that  conclusion much  sooner those two roses on his bicep one  of which appears to have a drop of blood  or tear falling from it  it just so happens that the names on the  ribbon translate to natasha  and elena as natasha and elena are  flying in to free alexi  their tablet showing the facility's  layout gives away his location  seventh circle prison fans of certain  marvel comics properties will know that  there is an eight issue run of the  daredevil  punisher team up series called seventh  circle but even though the black widow  has been associated with both of those  characters previously  it's unlikely that's the intended  reference it seems much more likely that  it's a reference to dante's divine  comedy more specifically inferno and  dante's 14th century poem  the seventh circle of hell is where  sinners who've committed violence are  tortured by centaurs and harpies  fans of classical greek mythology may  recall harpies  loathsome screeching creatures with the  head of a woman and the body of a great  bird harassed aeneas in virgil's epic  poem the aeneid  spoiling his crew's food so they could  not eat  that sure sounds like a certain pair of  prison guards who've stolen the baked  goods alexis fans have sent  him before his liberation from the  seventh circle prison alexi regales his  fellow inmates with the tales of his  glory days as the red guardian  marvel comics soviet russian foil to  captain america  as he nonchalantly takes on all comers  in arm wrestling  it's clearly a tale they've heard before  but one prisoner credited as muscular  gulag  inmate to avoid spoilers doesn't buy  alexi's story  pointing out that captain america was  still frozen when the story supposedly  took place  alexi isn't amused asking are you  calling me a liar ursa before slamming  the man's arm to the table breaking it  look at the big bear he says mockingly  it looks like we just met mikhail  ursus aka ursa major a soviet mutant who  is able to transform into a brown bear  it's not the last time alexi's heyday is  mocked  at molina's farm he tries to comfort  elena only to have his concern  rebuffed she says the only thing you  care about is your stupid glory days as  the crimson dynamo and no one wants to  hear about it  it appears to be meant as an insult with  yelena either mocking his former code  name or  actually forgetting it which alexi  corrects but elena has actually invoked  yet another russian marvel character one  we're  unlikely to see in the mcu in a version  faithful to the source material  why crimson dynamo was the name anton  vonko  father to iron man 2 villain ivan vonko  aka whiplash  took when wearing his own powered armor  as elena and natasha are holed up in the  rafters of a hungarian subway station  the two discussed the latter's previous  time hiding out in budapest nats already  made a reference to clint barton aka  hawkeye  and telling elena that the holes in the  safehouse walls were made by arrows not  bullets  she then reveals that she and barton  spent two days hiding out there  previously  at which point the camera shows a series  of games played on a ventilation duct  there are a few games of tic-tac-toe  into game of hangman  which someone seems to have lost it  seems to pretty clearly spell  butterfly but it wouldn't make for much  of an easter egg if it was that  straightforward  these insects have been cropping up in  the mcu with the butterflies in wand  division being the most recent example  perhaps the most direct connection  is to layla miller aka butterfly a  marvel comics mutant with a broad range  of abilities  one of her powers is the ability to  reanimate living things  but without restoring their souls it's  an intriguing reference given the  exchange on vormir in endgame in which  natasha traded her life to get clint the  soul stone  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  black widow are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

